  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 1.0,
    "cls_id": "CB02320",
    "sub_id": "43541",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": null,
    "tpa_score_new_en": "<div>Students are required to attend class. Each absent period means -1 attendance point. Anyone who altogether misses more than &gt;15&nbsp;periods during the semester automatically fails the course, unless there is a documented reason. Such situation will be dealt with on an individual basis.&nbsp;Each student needs to participate every week to get one point. This means direct communication with the teacher during lecturing time or classmates during their presentation. It can be done by commenting, answering or asking a question. Students need to actively take part in group work to gain one point each week. There will be an oral midterm assessment in the form of a discussion and an individual final presentation.</div>\n",
    "course_pol": null,
    "course_pol_en": "1. Be active in class. This is an integral part of the grade.\n2. Do not be late or leave early, otherwise it will be counted as absence.\n3. No bad language allowed or you are going to be asked to leave.\n4. Be polite to all people attending. Let us create a positive class atmosphere.\n5. Treat everyone with respect. Discrimination or harassment will be dealt with according to the university guidelines.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": "1. Every student needs to fulfill all parts of the class assessment.\n2. We are here to learn from each other.\n3. Do not hesitate to ask at any point, even after class.\n4. Please try to bring a good mood.\n5. If you do not like the course then simply drop it.",
    "ais_meno": null,
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>The purpose of this course is for students to actively learn and develop their critical thinking skills. What is valued most are students&#39; own analysis of discussed phenomenon and then putting forward their viewpoint. In other words creating a solid argument. It is discouraged to simply assume the ideas of others without giving them a proper thought. Cheating, copying or using AI for generating answers which are then presented as own ideas is absolutely forbidden. This will result in immediate expulsion from the course and is going to be reported to the university for further review.&nbsp;The same applies&nbsp;for cheating the online attendance system. All of the aforementioned&nbsp;actions will&nbsp;have serious consequences.</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
